+### `withoutQuery(input, keys)`
+
+Removes the given query parameter(s) from the URL, keeping everything else unchanged.
+
+If no parameters remain, the `?` is removed as well. Keys are matched after decoding.
+
+**Example:**
+
+```js
+withoutQuery("/foo?bar=1&baz=2", "bar"); // "/foo?baz=2"
+```
+
